[DONE] Friendly fire by ranged allies onto escort mission people sometimes makes them turn hostile, and actually counts as an attack against that whole city. For one, this should be accepted as a simple reality of battle by NPCs and not an intentional attack. Second, the town should not instantly turn against me — they would need a witness to properly deliver the news. We have the bones of that mechanic built, so we just need to incorporate it properly.
    Both halves were already built and neither was wired up, which the earlier
    note more or less predicted.
    THE ARROW KNEW AND THE IMPACT THREW IT AWAY. `applyDamage` takes an `incid`
    argument meaning "incidental", and two things downstream already honour it:
    a body is not `provoked` by an accident, and a townsperson's death is not a
    `civkill` if nobody chose it. The pyromancy splash four lines away has always
    passed `true`. But the projectile impact passed `false` unconditionally — so
    `p.ff`, computed at the moment of loosing by `fireRanged`, carried the whole
    length of the flight and was dropped on arrival. One argument.
    THE STANDING PENALTY HAD NO WITNESS CHECK AT ALL. `dropRep(d.homeTown, 4)`
    ran on every blow, wherever in the world it landed, whoever was or was not
    looking — in a file whose crime system opens with "nobody is wanted for what
    nobody saw". So a town could be furious about a thing it could not have
    arrested you for. It now runs `witnessNear`, the same machinery `crime` has
    always used.
    AND THE VICTIM IS NOT A BYSTANDER, which took a correction to get right.
    `applyDamage` runs that branch BEFORE the blow lands, so the person being
    shot is still `state === 'ok'` and was matching as their own witness — which
    made the gate vacuous for anyone caught alone, whatever happened to them a
    line later. `witnessNear` now takes a body to skip. `crime` deliberately
    keeps the old rule and still counts the victim: a BOUNTY is a thing the
    injured party can go and file, while what a town THINKS of you is what its
    people saw. Two different questions.
    Measured on the build before, staged as the report describes — an escort ward
    ninety tiles from any town, clipped by your own archer: "ward provoked true,
    hostile true, rep 0 -> -4". After: provoked false, hostile false, rep
    unchanged.
    Proof in tools/mishap.js, which fires real arrows through the real
    projectile mill and changes ONLY whether the shot was meant. Three controls
    green on both builds: an aimed shot in front of a witness still costs
    standing, they still turn on you for it, and one pair of eyes is still
    enough — because "accidents cost nothing" fixed too hard is just the
