[DONE] Speaking of escort missions, they pay INSANELY well when it's very far away. This is good as they are indeed the riskiest mission type, but their pay dwarfs every other. I think the solution is both to lower escort rewards a tad and also increase the reward for other mission types. (Sometimes it's literally just more profitable to sell the item they are asking for at their local market than to do the hand-in quest.)
    Measured before touching a number — 420 jobs of each kind rolled across
    every town on a real world. Median purse:
        supply 230 · nest bounty 980 · ESCORT 12,402
    Fifty-four times the one and twelve times the other. Nothing else on the
    board was worth reading, exactly as reported.
    THE CAUSE IS LINEAR DISTANCE. `300 + dist * 14` on a map 1440 tiles across,
    with towns sitting a median of 864 apart. Under a root instead — `420 +
    sqrt(dist) * 95` — the long haul still pays best, which is right, without
    being the only line on the post.
    And the other kinds came up as the note asked: a nest bounty to 1100-2100, a
    headcount to 210 a head.
    THE PARENTHESIS WAS THE SHARPER BUG and the earlier note was right that it is
    checkable on its own. 37 of 420 supply jobs paid LESS than selling the same
    goods to the same town — every one of them iron, where a high base price and
    a high town multiplier together beat a flat 0.75 of base. So the price is no
    longer guessed against `base`: it is set against the REAL LOCAL SALE PRICE
    with a premium on top, which makes the guarantee structural rather than a
    constant that happens to hold for most items. Median hand-in is now 3.34x
    what the goods would fetch, and 0 of 420 fall under.
    After: supply 436 · bounty 1470 · escort 3213. The escort is still the best
    purse on the board at 2.2x a bounty.
    Proof in tools/board.js, which asserts the SPREAD in both directions — a
    floor as well as a ceiling, since "escorts pay too much" fixed too hard
    becomes "escorts are not worth the risk", which is the same complaint upside
    down.

