    loads WITHOUT ERROR and quietly stops being anything: no label in the panel,
    no learn rates, no skin, no mesh. That reads as a corrupt save rather than
    as a line that was retired. `SUB_CUT` re-points them — Thinblood to
    Scaleborn (the plain line of that race; there is no other chimera caster and
    pretending otherwise would be worse), Cellar-line to Vat-born (general
    issue, no specialty, which is exactly what it now is) — and the load says so
    once, with a count, because somebody's named alchemist has just stopped
    learning magic the way it did yesterday.
    THE COVERAGE ARGUMENT DID NOT SURVIVE ITS OWN LINE. The homunculus block's
    comment justified the Cellar-line as the answer to farming and brewing
    having one line apiece. The Orchard-bred covers both and is the better line
    for it, being somebody's home rather than somebody's job. A line that exists
    to fill a column in a coverage table is a column in a coverage table, and
    the comment now says so.
    NO STREAM SHIFT. `rollSub` draws its number FIRST and maps it through the
