[DONE] There should be an easier way for a courting/wed couple to have kids.
Right now I do not see any means for them to actually do so, and I have waited
for many days in-game time. (Also: shack beds only fit one person, the model is
tiny, and there should be natural limits on procreation.)
    Proof in tools/kin2.js. 5 red on the build before, 0 after.
    IT ALREADY WORKED, WHICH IS THE WHOLE PROBLEM. Measured before changing a
    line: a staged wed couple standing together produced 5 pregnancies and 5
    births over 200 game-days, and with a house in the new build the first child
    arrives on DAY 14 against DAY 52 on the old one. At 2% a day that is a
    fifty-day wait, behind a test that both of them be within eight tiles AT THE
    MIDNIGHT TICK — which two people on different jobs frequently are not. The
    feature was invisible rather than absent, which is the worst way for one to
    be, and a probe asking "do births happen at all" would have been green the
    entire time.
    THE HOUSE IS THE FIX AND THE GATE AT ONCE. Build the couple a HOMESTEAD and
    the rate goes from one-in-fifty to one-in-eight and the proximity test
    becomes "are they both home", which two people who live somewhere are every
    night. Without one, nothing — a child needs a room, and that is a thing you
    can go and do something about, unlike a 2% roll you cannot see. Nobody else
    in the world is affected: the towns have their own roofs and were not what
    got reported.
    A HOMESTEAD RATHER THAN A BIGGER SHACK. A shack is a bunk somebody sleeps in
    between jobs and its healing bonus is balanced around being cheap, so it
    stays a bunk. The homestead is 4x4 against 3x3, lays FOUR beds against one —
    a double and two cots — and the model is a house: pitched roof, chimney with
    something burning in it, a step at the door and shutters, instead of the
    shack's cone hat.
    AND THE LIMITS ARE LIMITS AND NOT AN OFF SWITCH, which is asserted both ways:
    a full house (three) takes no more, a season must pass after each birth, and
    the SAME couple with room and off cooldown conceives five times in forty
    days. Without that last control a rule that simply blocked everything would
    have passed the first two.
    THE PROBE TIMED ITSELF OUT FIRST. It ran 1,320 day-rollovers to watch a house
    fill up, and a rollover is the heaviest tick in this game — every town, every
    civ, the whole economy. The limits being tested are a full house and a
    cooldown, so it sets each and shows nothing happens: same claim, forty days
    instead of nine hundred.
    AND IT WAS VERY NEARLY THE HOLDING CELL AGAIN. This file's own build list
    carries a note about that: costed, placeable, described, missing from
    `BUILD_CATS`, so it worked for every harness that called `placeStructure`
    directly and for nobody who played the game — 27 of 28 types listed, and the
    missing one was the one that got reported. The homestead is the 29th and I
    had done exactly the same thing. kin2.js asks the BUILD BAR for it now
    rather than the table.

