    member — at regard -25, which the panel reads as STRAINED. Every other ally
    in this game arrives already decided about you: the wanderers have a price,
    the drifters have a wage, the risen have no say. She arrives UNDECIDED, and
    -25 is chosen to sit a long way clear of the -60 where an ordinary mercenary
    starts packing, because a companion you can lose in one bad afternoon is a
    companion nobody takes out of camp.
    THE ARC READS THE WORLD, NOT A LEDGER. Seven beats, one at a time, two days
    apart minimum, each gated on a fact she could see for herself: a tear closed
    while she is standing in the specks, twelve of the dead walking behind you, a
    seat that bars its doors when it hears your name, the crown going on, seven
    halls signing the same page. That is the same source her greeting already
    read, which is why it stays honest — she is judging what is in front of her.
    BOTH ENDS ARE REAL, AND ONE OF THEM IS NOT A FAIL STATE. Past -45 she names
